  {"id":"A13","spot":13,"nums":{"t":6,"n":3},"q":"There are 6 times as many kids as teachers in the gym. There are 18 kids. How many teachers are in the gym?","choices":["3","12","24","6"],"answer":"3","slips":{"6":{"tag":"Picked a number from the problem","say":"6 is the times number. Share 18 into 6 equal groups. 18 ÷ 6 = 3."},"12":{"tag":"Subtracted instead of dividing","say":"You subtracted 18 − 6. Find the smaller amount by dividing. 18 ÷ 6 = 3."},"24":{"tag":"Added instead of dividing","say":"You added. Find the smaller amount by dividing. 18 ÷ 6 = 3."}},"hint":"Share 18 kids into 6 equal groups. One group is the teachers.","explanation":"Share 18 into 6 equal groups. 18 ÷ 6 = 3. Check: 6 × 3 = 18. There are 3 teachers.","explain":{"mult":{"top":"teachers","bottom":"kids","n":3,"t":6,"ask":null}}},
  {"id":"A14","spot":14,"nums":{"t":3,"n":5},"q":"Tom counts 5 tomato seeds. There are 3 times as many bean seeds as tomato seeds. Which equation can be used to find the number of bean seeds, b?","choices":["3 × 5 = b","3 + 5 = b","3 × b = 5","5 − 3 = b"],"answer":"3 × 5 = b","slips":{"3 + 5 = b":{"tag":"Picked the wrong sign","say":"That equation adds. Times as many means using multiplication to compare. 3 × 5 = b."},"3 × b = 5":{"tag":"Put the unknown in the wrong place","say":"b is the bigger amount, the answer. 5 is the smaller amount. 3 × 5 = b."},"5 − 3 = b":{"tag":"Picked the wrong sign","say":"That equation subtracts. Times as many means using multiplication to compare. 3 × 5 = b."}},"hint":"There are 3 groups of 5. Use ×.","explanation":"3 times as many as 5 means 3 × 5. So 3 × 5 = b.","explain":{"mult":{"top":"tomato seeds","bottom":"bean seeds","n":5,"t":3,"ask":"letter","letter":"b"}}},
  {"id":"A15","spot":15,"nums":{"t":2,"n":8},"q":"Dan has 8 cards. Nina has 2 times as many cards as Dan. Which equation can be used to find the number of cards, c, for Nina?","choices":["2 × 8 = c","2 + 8 = c","2 × c = 8","8 − 2 = c"],"answer":"2 × 8 = c","slips":{"2 + 8 = c":{"tag":"Picked the wrong sign","say":"That equation adds. Times as many means using multiplication to compare. 2 × 8 = c."},"2 × c = 8":{"tag":"Put the unknown in the wrong place","say":"c is the bigger amount, the answer. 8 is the smaller amount. 2 × 8 = c."},"8 − 2 = c":{"tag":"Picked the wrong sign","say":"That equation subtracts. Times as many means using multiplication to compare. 2 × 8 = c."}},"hint":"Nina has 2 groups of 8. Use ×.","explanation":"2 times as many as 8 means 2 × 8. So 2 × 8 = c.","explain":{"mult":{"top":"Dan","bottom":"Nina","n":8,"t":2,"ask":"letter","letter":"c"}}},
  {"id":"A16","spot":16,"nums":{"t":2,"n":8},"q":"On Saturday, Owen did 16 jumping jacks. That is 2 times as many jumping jacks as on Tuesday. Part A: Which equation can be used to find how many jumping jacks, j, Owen did on Tuesday?","choices":["16 ÷ 2 = j","16 × 2 = j","16 − 2 = j","16 + 2 = j"],"answer":"16 ÷ 2 = j","slips":{"16 × 2 = j":{"tag":"Multiplied instead of dividing","say":"Tuesday had fewer jumping jacks. 16 is 2 times as many. Divide: 16 ÷ 2 = j."},"16 − 2 = j":{"tag":"Picked the wrong sign","say":"Times as many is not take away. Divide to find the smaller amount: 16 ÷ 2 = j."},"16 + 2 = j":{"tag":"Picked the wrong sign","say":"Tuesday had fewer. Divide to find the smaller amount: 16 ÷ 2 = j."}},"hint":"Tuesday had the smaller amount. 16 is 2 groups of that amount.","explanation":"16 jumping jacks on Saturday is 2 times as many as on Tuesday. Divide to find the smaller amount: 16 ÷ 2 = j.","explain":{"mult":{"top":"Tuesday","bottom":"Saturday","n":"j","t":2,"ask":"small","total":16}}},
  {"id":"A17","spot":17,"nums":{"t":2,"n":8},"q":"On Saturday, Owen did 16 jumping jacks. That is 2 times as many jumping jacks as on Tuesday. Part B: How many jumping jacks did Owen do on Tuesday?","choices":["8","14","32","18"],"answer":"8","slips":{"14":{"tag":"Subtracted instead of dividing","say":"You subtracted 16 − 2. Divide: 16 ÷ 2 = 8."},"18":{"tag":"Added instead of dividing","say":"You added. Tuesday had fewer. Divide: 16 ÷ 2 = 8."},"32":{"tag":"Multiplied instead of dividing","say":"You multiplied. Tuesday had fewer. Divide: 16 ÷ 2 = 8."}},"hint":"Use your equation from Part A. Divide 16 by 2.","explanation":"16 ÷ 2 = 8. Check: 2 × 8 = 16. Owen did 8 jumping jacks on Tuesday.","explain":{"mult":{"top":"Tuesday","bottom":"Saturday","n":8,"t":2,"ask":null}}}
